# Lapis Cloud -- STAGING instance coturn config. This is a TEMPLATE, not the real file: the
# placeholders below are substituted from deploy/production-staging/.env by render-secrets.sh (see
# ../production/README.adoc "Video conferencing"). The rendered turnserver.conf is gitignored --
# never commit it.
#
# `realm` and `min-port`/`max-port` are staging's own disjoint values -- see
# ../production-elb/turnserver.conf.template's own comment for why the relay range specifically
# must equal the externally-published range (51040-51059 here, see docker-compose.yml).
# `listening-port` stays 3478 (safe to remap on the host side only -- 3480 here).
listening-port=3478
min-port=51040
max-port=51059
realm=staging.parteidervernunft.de
use-auth-secret
static-auth-secret=${LAPIS_TURN_SECRET}
external-ip=${LAPIS_PUBLIC_IP}
no-dtls
fingerprint
log-file=stdout
no-cli

# ── TURNS over TLS (optional, DISABLED BY DEFAULT) -- see README.adoc "TURNS over TLS" (Offene
# Frage O-3 there: only set this up if the staging instance is meant to exercise the TURNS path
# too). Unlike ../production/'s own copy of this block, this one is commented out by default: PdV's
# `/usr/local/sbin/sync-turn-certs.sh` (run by the `sync-turn-certs.timer` systemd timer) is not set
# up to also populate `deploy/production-staging/coturn-certs/` (which ships with only a .gitkeep),
# so on a fresh install `cert`/`pkey` below would point at files that do not exist -- coturn then
# either logs "Bad configuration format" and silently refuses to start the TLS listener (see
# ../production/turnserver.conf.template's own comment for the wrong-key-name variant of this
# failure), or fails to start at all, and nothing in the docs flags this. Uncomment the three lines
# below only AFTER wiring a certificate sync for this instance (e.g. extending
# sync-turn-certs.sh/its timer to also copy into `coturn-certs/` here). `tls-listening-port` stays
# 5350 CONTAINER-side; the host-side publish is 5352 here (docker-compose.yml).
# tls-listening-port=5350
# cert=/etc/coturn/certs/turn-fullchain.pem
# pkey=/etc/coturn/certs/turn-privkey.pem
